{#=============================================================================
  _estate_glyphs.html.j2 — the calculator glyph family (Free Estate)

  ONE bespoke line-art glyph per calculator, in the macro terminal idiom:
  hairline strokes (stroke-width ~1.6, round caps, non-scaling), monochrome +
  ONE --link accent, small. Each glyph *represents its calculator's concept* so
  the six read as distinct at a glance while sharing one drawing grammar — a
  family, not six unrelated icons. Replaces the old single zigzag ".tc-plot"
  that every card and card-crown shared.

  ── USAGE ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    {% import "_estate_glyphs.html.j2" as glyphs %}
    {{ glyphs.glyph('position-size', 'card') }}   → 56×36 hub-card corner glyph
    {{ glyphs.glyph('position-size', 'crown') }}  → 620×64 calculator-card crown

  Both variants share the same viewBox+geometry; the wrapper class differs
  (.egl-card vs .egl-crown, styled in seo_base). The dotted "ink" that traces on
  reveal is class .egl-draw; static furniture is .egl-still; the single accent
  mark (arrow head, node, cap) is .egl-mark. All respect prefers-reduced-motion
  (see .egl CSS in seo_base).

  ── ADDING A GLYPH FOR A NEW CALCULATOR (the 20-more path) ────────────────────
    1. Add one `{% macro _g_<slug_underscored>() %}…{% endmacro %}` below,
       drawing INSIDE the shared 0 0 64 40 viewBox (keep to ~4..60 x, ~6..34 y).
       Use <path class="egl-draw"> for the traced line, <path class="egl-still">
       for context furniture, and ONE .egl-mark for the accent (node/arrow/cap).
    2. Register it in the _GLYPHS dispatch map at the bottom (slug → macro).
    3. Nothing else — hub cards call glyphs.glyph(slug,'card') by the registry
       slug; a calculator page overrides {% block calc_glyph %} to call
       glyphs.glyph('<slug>','crown'). If a slug is missing, glyph() falls back
       to the neutral _g_default (a calm baseline) — never errors.

  Concept per glyph (why each looks the way it does):
    position-size      → stacked share-columns capped by a shielded stop line
    risk-reward        → opposing bars, small risk (1↓) : larger reward (2↑)
    trade-profit       → an entry line, long up-arrow & short down-arrow diverge
    compounding        → an accelerating exponential "snowball" curve
    cagr               → a smooth growth ramp between two marked points
    drawdown-recovery  → a peak, a valley dip, then a climb back to the peak
=============================================================================#}

